/-
# Critical horizon: full geometric monodromy of the raw/reciprocal observation map

Bundles the `HTGeometry.Critical` development. For positive horizon depths `m, n` and an
algebraically closed characteristic-zero field `K`, the critical source field is generated by the raw
jet coordinates `x_0, ..., x_(m+n-1)`, and the critical observation field by the raw tail from index
`m` and the reciprocal tail from index `n`. The submodules build the observation and source charts,
the rectangular-Schur ramification divisor, reduction of geometric sheets at the Schur place,
monodromy blocks with their normalizations, and the raw and reciprocal coordinate valuations.
Together they show that the Schur place has ramification index two with inertia of order two acting
as a transposition, that the extension degree equals the critical binomial multiplicity, that the
monodromy action is primitive (purity of block normalizations plus two explicit source meridians),
and hence (`criticalGeometricMonodromy_eq_top_charZero`) that the geometric monodromy group is the
full symmetric group on the geometric sheets. These final results are unconditional for `0 < m`,
`0 < n`.
-/

